# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vle-extension-vendor-divergences -- VLE-* edge semantics as BricsCAD does
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: windows-runner-sunset-probe-campaign
#+BRANCH: fix-b1-b2-divergences
#+DATE: 2026-10-29

Measured by the sunset campaign's B2 probe (probes/sources/probe-vle.lsp) on
real hardware 2026-10-24: AutoCAD 2022 + BricsCAD V26, committed under
probe-results/{autocad/ms-windows/20261024T201442Z,bricscad/macos/20261024T201604Z}/.

The VLE-* family is a BricsCAD extension: AutoCAD returns "no function
definition" for every one of them, which CONFIRMS the Availability line
(BricsCAD-only) on all nine probed symbols. The behaviour therefore comes from
BricsCAD V26, and clautolisp -- as the implementation of a BricsCAD extension --
should match it. Of the nine SPEC-UNCERTAIN markers probed, five already agree
with BricsCAD; four diverge.

* Already correct (markers can close to Vendor-cited)
- vle-subst-nth out-of-range IDX -> list unchanged.
- vle-list-split -> 2-list (head tail), splitter dropped; at head -> (nil (a b c));
  not present -> ((a b c) nil).
- vle-string-replace -> replace ALL; empty new-str deletes.
- vle-string-split -> empty tokens between adjacent delimiters KEPT.

* Diverging from BricsCAD

** vle-member -- returns the tail, BricsCAD returns T/nil  [FIXED this branch]
=(vle-member 'b '(a b c))= is =T= on BricsCAD, =(vle-member 'z ...)= is nil;
clautolisp returned the tail =(b c)=. Adopt the boolean (the tail is still
reachable via VLE-SEARCH, which is unchanged). Low risk: truthy either way in
IF/WHILE; only code pulling the tail from vle-member specifically is affected,
and vle-search covers that.

** vle-vector-normalise -- zero input: nil vs zero vector  [FIXED this branch]
=(vle-vector-normalise '(0 0 0))= is =(0.0 0.0 0.0)= on BricsCAD; clautolisp
returned nil. Adopt the zero vector.

** vle-rgb2aci -- argument shape  [TODO: owner decision + arity change]
BricsCAD accepts a single packed INTEGER (=(vle-rgb2aci 255)= -> 1) and THREE
ints (=(vle-rgb2aci 255 0 0)= -> 1), and REJECTS the (R G B) LIST form.
clautolisp accepts ONLY the list. Needs: accept int (packed 24-bit) and the
3-arg form; and a decision on whether to KEEP the list form as a clautolisp
lenient extension or reject it like BricsCAD. Arity change + the existing test
(m3c-vle-rgb2aci-nearest-known asserts the list form) make this the owner's call.

** vle-aci2rgb -- the 10-249 algorithmic range  [TODO: needs the full palette]
BricsCAD returns real RGB across 10-249 (sampled: 10 -> (255 0 0), 150 ->
(0 127 255), 249 -> (76 38 47)); clautolisp returns nil there (only 0-9 / 250-255
tabulated). Three samples are not the table -- this needs the full 256-entry ACI
palette, either probed exhaustively (extend probe-vle.lsp to sweep 0..255 on
BricsCAD) or sourced from the documented ACI scheme. Deferred until the table
exists.

* vle-vector-getucs -- not compared to clautolisp here
The B2 probe captured BricsCAD's basis for +Z/-Z/near-Z normals; the AutoCAD-vs-
BricsCAD diff did not include a clautolisp column for getucs, so whether
clautolisp agrees is unverified. Re-run probe-vle.lsp's clautolisp baseline and
compare before deciding.

* Status

TODO. vle-member and vle-vector-normalise are FIXED on branch
fix-b1-b2-divergences (adopt the measured BricsCAD behaviour; markers flipped to
Vendor cites; tests updated; version bumped). vle-rgb2aci (arity + list-form
decision) and vle-aci2rgb (full palette) remain, plus the getucs baseline check.
